    "+ is check, # is checkmate: Qh5#." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "+ je šach, # je mat: Dh5#."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "=Q is a promotion: e8=Q. A file letter is added when two pieces could reach the square: Nbd2." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "=D je proměna: e8=D. Když by na pole mohly jít dvě stejné figury, přidá se písmeno sloupce: Jbd2."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 — the moves that reached this position." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "1.e4 e5 2.Jf3 — tahy, které vedly k této pozici."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "3 minutes" : {
      "comment" : "Puzzle rush kind",
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "3 minuty"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "5 minutes" : {
      "comment" : "Puzzle rush kind",
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "5 minut"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "50 moves without a capture or pawn move." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "50 tahů bez braní a bez tahu pěšcem."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "64 squares, and how they are named" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "64 polí a jak se jmenují"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A balanced opponent" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Vyrovnaný soupeř"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A ballpark from your results against the computer levels — not an official rating." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Hrubý odhad z vašich výsledků proti úrovním počítače — není to oficiální rating."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A bishop slides any distance along a diagonal, as long as nothing stands in the way. Because it moves diagonally it can never change square colour: one of your bishops lives on light squares for the whole game, the other on dark ones." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Střelec klouže po diagonále jak daleko chce, pokud mu nic nestojí v cestě. Protože táhne šikmo, nikdy nezmění barvu pole: jeden váš střelec zůstane celou partii na světlých polích, druhý na tmavých."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A blunder. %@ was far better.%@" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Hrubka. %@ byl mnohem lepší.%@"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A check can be answered by moving the king away, by blocking the line between the attacker and the king, or by capturing the attacker. If none of them is possible, the game is over." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Na šach se dá odpovědět odchodem krále, zaclonením linie mezi útočníkem a králem, nebo sebráním útočníka. Pokud nejde nic z toho, partie končí."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A check from a knight cannot be blocked — a knight jumps." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Šach jezdcem nelze zaclonit — jezdec skáče."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A few more patterns" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Několik dalších motivů"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A fork attacks two things at once. Your opponent can only save one of them, so the other is yours. Knights are the great forkers, because their jump attacks squares that no other piece would guard." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Vidlička napadá dvě věci najednou. Soupeř může zachránit jen jednu, druhá je vaše. Největšími mistry vidliček jsou jezdci, protože jejich skok napadá pole, která by žádná jiná figura nekryla."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A game on the clock can also be lost on time: run out and you lose — unless your opponent has nothing left to mate with, which makes it a draw." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Partii na čas lze prohrát i na čas: komu dojde čas, prohrává — ledaže soupeři nezbylo nic, čím by mohl dát mat; pak je to remíza."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A game that neither side can win is a draw, worth half a point to each player. Four of them the app spots by itself and tells you which one happened; the fifth is yours to settle — the Draw button under the board." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Partie, kterou nemůže vyhrát ani jedna strana, je remíza za půl bodu pro každého. Čtyři z nich aplikace pozná sama a řekne vám, která nastala; pátou si domluvíte sami — tlačítkem Remíza pod šachovnicí."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A green arrow shows the move the engine would have preferred." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Zelená šipka ukazuje tah, kterému by engine dal přednost."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A king already stands on the hill." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Král už stojí na kopci."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A king and one bishop can never force mate — dead drawn." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Král a jeden střelec mat nikdy nevynutí — mrtvá remíza."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A knight in the centre reaches eight squares; in the corner, only two." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Jezdec ve středu dosáhne na osm polí, v rohu jen na dvě."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A known opening move" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Známý tah ze zahájení"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A lone queen or rook plus king is enough to mate; a lone bishop or knight is not." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Samotná dáma nebo věž s králem na mat stačí, samotný střelec nebo jezdec ne."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A merciless machine" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Nemilosrdný stroj"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A mistake. %@ was clearly better.%@" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Chyba. %@ byl zřetelně lepší.%@"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A move is written as the letter of the piece and the square it goes to: Nf3 is a knight to f3, Qd8 a queen to d8. Pawns have no letter, so e4 simply means a pawn moved to e4. The knight is N, because K is taken by the king." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Tah se zapisuje jako písmeno figury a pole, na které jde: Jf3 je jezdec na f3, Dd8 dáma na d8. Pěšci písmeno nemají, takže e4 znamená prostě pěšce na e4. Každý jazyk má vlastní písmena — čeština píše J, D, V, S a K."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A new puzzle every day" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Každý den nová úloha"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A new puzzle is waiting · %lld-day streak" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "variations" : {
            "plural" : {
              "few" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "Čeká nová úloha · %lld dny v řadě"
                }
              },
              "one" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "Čeká nová úloha · %lld den v řadě"
                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "Čeká nová úloha · %lld dní v řadě"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "variations" : {
            "plural" : {
              "one" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "A new puzzle is waiting · %lld-day streak"
                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "A new puzzle is waiting · %lld-day streak"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A pawn plods one square straight forward. From its starting square it may jump two squares instead. A pawn can never move backwards, and it cannot move forward onto an occupied square — not even to capture." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Pěšec se sune o jedno pole rovně vpřed. Z výchozího pole může místo toho skočit o dvě. Zpátky nemůže nikdy a na obsazené pole před sebou nevstoupí — ani braním."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A pawn takes one square diagonally forward. So it moves in one direction and captures in another — which is why pawns lock each other up head to head and yet guard each other so well side by side." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Pěšec bere o jedno pole šikmo vpřed. Táhne tedy jedním směrem a bere jiným — proto se proti sobě zablokují a přitom se vedle sebe tak dobře kryjí."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A pawn that jumps two squares to slip past an enemy pawn can be taken anyway, as if it had only moved one square. This capture — en passant, \"in passing\" — is available on the very next move and never again." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Pěšce, který skočí o dvě pole, aby proklouzl kolem soupeřova pěšce, lze přesto vzít, jako by táhl jen o jedno. Tohle braní — en passant, „mimochodem“ — je možné jen bezprostředně následujícím tahem a nikdy později."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A pawn that reaches the far side of the board turns into a queen, rook, bishop or knight of its own colour — your choice, and you can have as many queens as you can promote pawns. Almost everybody takes the queen." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Pěšec, který dojde na druhý konec šachovnice, se promění v dámu, věž, střelce nebo jezdce své barvy — podle vaší volby, a dam můžete mít tolik, kolik pěšců doženete. Skoro každý si bere dámu."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A piece in the middle of the board controls more squares than one at the edge, and pawns in the centre take space away from your opponent. That is why almost every opening starts with 1.e4 or 1.d4." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Figura uprostřed šachovnice kontroluje víc polí než na kraji a pěšci ve středu berou soupeři prostor. Proto skoro každé zahájení začíná 1.e4 nebo 1.d4."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A pinned piece cannot move without exposing the king behind it — so, in the eyes of the rules, it often cannot move at all. Pin a defender and it stops defending; then pile more attackers onto it." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Vázaná figura nemůže odejít, aniž by vystavila krále za sebou — takže podle pravidel často nemůže táhnout vůbec. Zavažte obránce a přestane bránit; pak na něj přiveďte další útočníky."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A rook slides any distance along a rank or a file. It is at its best on an open file, where nothing blocks it, and on the seventh rank, where it attacks the enemy pawns from behind." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Věž klouže jak daleko chce po řadě nebo po sloupci. Nejlépe se jí daří na otevřeném sloupci, kde jí nic nebrání, a na sedmé řadě, odkud napadá soupeřovy pěšce zezadu."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A sacrifice that works" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Oběť, která vychází"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A sacrifice that works — the %@ is offered and the initiative more than pays for it." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Oběť, která vychází — dává v sázku %@ a iniciativa to bohatě vynahradí."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A sacrifice that works — the %@ is offered, and it forces a win in %lld." : {
      "comment" : "Review, King of the Hill or Three-check; the number is the move the win comes on",
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Oběť, která vychází — dává v sázku %@ a vynucuje výhru %lld. tahem."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A sacrifice that works — the %@ is offered, and it forces mate in %lld." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Oběť, která vychází — dává v sázku %@ a vynucuje mat %lld. tahem."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A selection from the Lichess puzzle database, released into the public domain under CC0. Bundled with the app, so they work without a connection." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Výběr z databáze úloh Lichess, uvolněné jako volné dílo pod licencí CC0. Jsou přibalené v aplikaci, takže fungují i bez připojení."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A skewer is a pin the other way round: the valuable piece is in front and has to move, and what stands behind it falls. Checks are the sharpest skewers, because the king has no choice." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Napíchnutí je vazba naopak: vpředu stojí cennější figura, ta musí odejít a padne to, co stálo za ní. Nejostřejší napíchnutí jsou se šachem, protože král nemá na výběr."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A sound move. %@ was a little stronger." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Solidní tah. %@ byl o něco silnější."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A square is named after its file and its rank. The square where the e-file crosses the fourth rank is e4. That is how chess moves are written, and it is how the move list in this app reads." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Pole se jmenuje podle svého sloupce a řady. Pole, kde se sloupec e kříží se čtvrtou řadou, je e4. Přesně tak se zapisují šachové tahy a tak je čte i seznam tahů v této aplikaci."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A tough nut to crack" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Tvrdý oříšek"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A winning chance went by" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Šance na výhru utekla"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A won position slipped: %@ was the way through.%@" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Vyhraná pozice utekla: %@ byla cesta k výhře.%@"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "ACCURACY" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "PŘESNOST"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "accuracy.spoken" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver summary of a player's accuracy card",
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "přesnost %1$@ procenta, %2$@"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%@ percent accuracy, %@"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Achievement earned" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Získán úspěch"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Achievements" : {
      "comment" : "My Games tab",
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Úspěchy"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Adaptive" : {
      "comment" : "Difficulty level that adjusts to the player",
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Adaptivní"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Advanced pawn" : {
      "comment" : "Puzzle theme",
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Postoupený pěšec"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "After 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bc4 Bc5 — both sides developing." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Po 1.e4 e5 2.Jf3 Jc6 3.Sc4 Sc5 — obě strany vyvíjejí."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "After castling, giving your king one free square in front of the pawns is worth a move." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Po rošádě stojí za jeden tah udělat králi před pěšci volné pole."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Agree to a Draw" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Dohodnout remízu"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Agree to a draw?" : {
      "comment" : "Confirmation before ending a two-player game as a draw",
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Dohodnout remízu?"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Agreement: both players simply settle for a draw — the Draw button, in a game of two players." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Dohoda: hráči se na remíze prostě domluví — tlačítkem Remíza v partii dvou hráčů."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "ahead by %lld" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver: material advantage in pawns",
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "vede o %lld"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Ahead in material: trade pieces, head for the endgame." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Máte navíc: vyměňujte figury a miřte do koncovky."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Albin Counter-Gambit" : {
      "comment" : "Chess opening",
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Albinův protigambit"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Alekhine Defense" : {
      "comment" : "Chess opening",
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Alechinova obrana"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "All" : {
      "comment" : "Game list filter",
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Vše"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "All %lld lessons read" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Přečteno všech %lld lekcí"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "All six pieces, one at a time" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Všech šest figur, jedna po druhé"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Almost every material win comes from one of a handful of ideas. Once you know their names you start seeing them." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Skoro každý zisk materiálu vychází z hrstky nápadů. Jakmile znáte jejich jména, začnete je vidět."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Analysis Board" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Analytická šachovnice"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Analyze" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Analyzovat"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Analyze this position" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Analyzovat tuto pozici"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Analyzing your game…" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Analyzuji vaši partii…"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "announce.achievement" : {
      "comment" : "Spoken when an achievement is earned",
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Získán úspěch: %@"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Achievement earned: %@"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "announce.bookMove" : {
      "comment" : "Spoken when the opening trainer shows the expected move, e.g. 'The book move is knight f 3.'",
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Teoretický tah je %@."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The book move is %@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "announce.flag" : {
      "comment" : "Spoken when a flag falls on the chess clock",
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%@: čas vypršel"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%@'s time is up"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "announce.hint" : {
      "comment" : "Spoken when a hint is shown, e.g. 'Hint: knight f 3'",
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Nápověda: %@"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Hint: %@"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "announce.lessonMoveSpoken" : {
      "comment" : "Spoken after a move is played on a lesson diagram, e.g. 'Played knight f 3'",
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Zahráno: %@"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Played %@"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "announce.lowTime" : {
      "comment" : "Spoken when a player's clock runs low, e.g. 'White: 10 seconds left'",
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%@: zbývá %@"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%@: %@ left"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "announce.moveSpoken" : {
      "comment" : "Spoken after a move is made: the side, then the move, e.g. 'White: knight f 3'",
      "localizations" : {
        "cs" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%1$@: %2$@"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%@: %@"
          }
        }
      }
